\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Kho'ini (also Xoini, Khoeini, Di; ISO 639-3 xkc; Glottolog khoi1250) is a Tatic Northwestern Iranian language (Indo-European). It is spoken in and around the village of Xoin, roughly 60 km southwest of Zanjan, Iran. Sources describe it as endangered, with Azeri Turkish now dominant locally. The most recent data cited in the sources I found date from the early 1960s. Whether it is a language or a dialect is disputed. I found no school materials in it.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
I found no primers, textbooks or school programmes for Kho'ini in the search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, ``Kho'ini dialect'': a general overview of classification and location. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kho%27ini_dialect}
\item Verbix Endangered Languages page on Khoini: a short descriptive entry. \url{https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Khoini}
\item Endangered Languages Project entry: a status record, not checked in detail. \url{https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/3252?hl=es}
\item Glottolog entry for khoi1250, for classification and bibliography. \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/khoi1250.bigmap.html}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
I found no scripture translations or community organisations specific to Kho'ini.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
I found no audio, video or corpus resources for Kho'ini.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Little documentation exists, and the sources suggest the language is disappearing in favour of Turkish. Any curriculum would need fresh fieldwork with remaining speakers, using the Glottolog bibliography to locate early descriptions. This dossier is a starting point, not a resource base.

\end{document}
